{"timestamp": 1779426103.7088356, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 19, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I found Charlie's body in Electrical just now. My route this round was pretty long: I started around Upper Engine, went to Oxygen, down to Lower Engine, back up to Upper Engine, then through Medbay, and finally into Electrical where I found him. \n\nI saw Charlie alive very early on in Upper Engine. More recently, I bumped into Bob in Upper Engine around tick 16, and then I saw Frank in Medbay right before I walked into Electrical (around tick 18). \n\nI didn't see anyone running out of Electrical when I got there. Frank, since you were right next door in Medbay, did you see anyone heading that way? Also, it looks like Diana is dead too \u2014 does anyone have information on her? Let's get our info out there."}}
{"timestamp": 1779426127.8711662, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 19, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I passed through Electrical earlier, but not near the report. Around tick 9 I saw Bob and Charlie both in Electrical, and Charlie was still there when I left. I specifically saw Bob leave Electrical toward Medbay around tick 10. After that I went through Security, down to Navigation, then over to Storage where I was when the report happened.\n\nFor Diana, I only saw her early in Weapons around tick 5, so if she died later I don\u2019t have much. But for Charlie\u2019s body being in Electrical, the last people I can place around him are Bob and me earlier \u2014 and I left toward Security/Navigation, not back into Electrical. Bob leaving toward Medbay is worth checking with Frank/Eve\u2019s timing."}}
{"timestamp": 1779426148.640987, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 19, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "My route this round was Lower Engine, then Upper Engine, Oxygen, Cafeteria, and finally Medbay. \n\nEve, I can completely verify the end of your route. I was in Medbay, and I saw you enter from Upper Engine at tick 18 and walk straight into Electrical, right before the report popped up. Unless you killed Charlie the exact millisecond you stepped in, it's highly likely Charlie was already dead when you found him. \n\nLooking at the timeline Alice provided, Charlie was in Electrical around tick 9 with Bob. Alice saw Bob leave towards Medbay at tick 10, and Eve later saw Bob in Upper Engine at tick 16. That means Bob was one of the last people with Charlie and moved right through the area where the body was later found. \n\nWe also have no idea where Diana's body is, which means a double kill happened this round. Bob, you are speaking last. You need to explain exactly what you did after leaving Electrical, and whether you saw Diana anywhere on your way to Upper Engine. Right now, you are the prime suspect for Charlie's death, but I'm going to listen to your defense before I lock in a vote."}}
{"timestamp": 1779426166.3189242, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 19, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Frank, Eve, listen carefully because Alice is twisting the truth to frame me. \n\nMy route was Weapons -> Security -> Electrical -> Medbay -> Upper Engine. \n\nAlice is right that we were both in Electrical with Charlie around tick 9 and 10. She entered Electrical from Security at tick 9. However, when I left Electrical towards Medbay, I left ALICE AND CHARLIE ALONE in that room. I didn't leave Charlie by himself; I left him with Alice. She is trying to make it sound like I was the last person with him, but she was! \n\nSince I went to Medbay and Upper Engine (and Eve confirms seeing me in Upper Engine at tick 16), I was far away from Electrical. Alice had every opportunity to kill Charlie the moment I walked out.\n\nAs for Diana, I saw Diana leave Security heading towards Weapons at tick 4. Alice just admitted she saw Diana in Weapons around tick 5. \n\nIt all perfectly aligns for Alice being the Duck: She killed Diana in Weapons early on, made her way down through Security to Electrical by tick 9, waited for me to leave, and then killed Charlie. \n\nAlice is the Duck. Vote Alice."}}
{"timestamp": 1779426257.014828, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 19, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "Alice"}}
{"timestamp": 1779426314.1558404, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 19, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "Bob is doing exactly what I expected once Frank put pressure on him: turn it into a 50/50 and say I\u2019m \u201ctwisting\u201d things.\n\nYes, after Bob left Electrical toward Medbay, I was briefly still there with Charlie \u2014 but Charlie was alive when I left. I went out toward Security, then Navigation/Storage, and I was nowhere near Electrical when Eve found the body. Bob saying he was \u201cfar away\u201d at tick 16 doesn\u2019t clear him at all; he had plenty of time after leaving Electrical at tick 10 to double back or do the kill before ending up Upper Engine.\n\nAlso, Bob\u2019s Diana theory is really convenient. He places himself Weapons/Security early, which is exactly the area Diana was last seen. I openly gave that I saw Diana in Weapons around tick 5 \u2014 if I were trying to hide a kill there, I wouldn\u2019t be volunteering that last-seen info.\n\nThe solid chain we have is: Bob was with Charlie in Electrical, left toward Medbay, had a big gap, and later Charlie is dead in Electrical. Eve and Frank basically clear each other for the report timing. That leaves Bob as the best vote. I\u2019m voting Bob."}}
{"timestamp": 1779426334.114307, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 19, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "This is a classic he-said-she-said, but Alice, your own defense actually makes you look worse. You just admitted that Bob left Electrical *before* you did, which means you were the last person to be alone with Charlie. You had the perfect opportunity to kill him right after Bob walked out, before you headed down to Security. \n\nBob's timeline also checks out with Eve seeing him in Upper Engine at tick 16. If Bob killed Charlie at tick 10, he would have had to immediately flee to Upper Engine, which is possible, but you being alone with Charlie is a smoking gun. Furthermore, Bob's theory about Diana dying in Weapons makes a lot of sense, considering you were the last one to see her there. \n\nEve is voting Alice, Alice is voting Bob. I'm the deciding vote here, and based on the fact that Alice was definitively the last person with the victim, my vote is going to Alice."}}
